{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The IvorGeneralMIDI framework provides the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/midi.org\/general-midi","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and General MIDI 2 sound sets as Swift","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"enumerations. For General MIDI 1: the 128 instruments that a program change","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"selects, the 16 instrument families they fall into, and the 47 sounds of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"percussion key map. For General MIDI 2: the 256 instruments that a bank select","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and program change select, the 9 drum sets, and the 61 sounds of the extended","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"percussion key map. Each sound can be looked up by its program, bank, or note,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or by its name as the specification gives it, and converted back again.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Programs, notes, and channels use the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/eBardX\/IvorMIDI","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" data value types, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorGeneralMIDI\/documentation\/IvorGeneralMIDI\/GMMessage","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" covers the system exclusive messages that turn General MIDI on and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"off, and the General MIDI 2 effects and controllers."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import IvorGeneralMIDI","","let guitar = GM1Instrument(program: 25)","","guitar              \/\/ .acousticGuitarNylon","guitar.name         \/\/ \"Acoustic Guitar (nylon)\"","guitar.family       \/\/ 